.TH "tangsible" "1" "2026-09-05" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible - a live terminal UI for ansible-playbook
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR \fIverb\fR [\fIargs\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR wraps \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) in a live, navigable tree of plays → tasks → hosts.\& It comes up immediately and updates live while the playbook is still running, and lets you drill into any host'\&s result — task source, output, stderr, \fB--diff\fR output, full JSON — without losing your place in the run.\&
.PP
It is a development and troubleshooting interface for \fBansible-playbook\fR, not a replacement for it or an orchestration platform.\& It is aimed at someone running playbooks by hand, repeatedly, against a live-ish environment — not at CI pipelines, scheduled automation, or fleet-scale inventories.\&
.PP
In addition, tangsible provides useful utilities to rerun / analyze previous playbook runs, debug Jinja2 template, get host information and easily edit individually encrypted variables.\&
.PP
Every \fIverb\fR below is documented in its own manual page.\& This page covers what all of them have in common: configuration, environment variables, and files.\&
.PP
.SH VERBS
.PP
\fBtangsible-run\fR(1)
.RS 4
Run a playbook and show its live progress in the tree UI.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-rerun\fR(1)
.RS 4
Run a previous playbook again.\& Hosts, tags, starting play and other parameters can be modified compared to the previous run.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-role\fR(1)
.RS 4
Run a single role in isolation, without hand-writing a wrapper playbook.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-template\fR(1)
.RS 4
Render one Jinja2 template through Ansible'\&s own templating engine, against an existing inventory host.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-host\fR(1)
.RS 4
Show everything Tangsible can determine about one host: live facts, inventory group membership, which plays would run, host_vars, and the raw \fBansible-inventory --host\fR dump.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-hosts\fR(1)
.RS 4
Browse all inventory host, then drill into any one of them with the same view \fBtangsible host\fR shows.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-revisit\fR(1)
.RS 4
Browse previous runs and reopen one, then analyze all information exactly as it looked when it finished.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible-vault\fR(1)
.RS 4
Edit individually vault-encrypted variables in a file in place, without hand-running \fBansible-vault encrypt_string\fR and pasting ciphertext back yourself.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtangsible version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information about tangsible and all components it'\&s using.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR requires \fBansible-playbook\fR and the jsonl plugin from the \fBansible.\&posix\fR collection to be installed and on \fBPATH\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ansible-galaxy collection install ansible\&.posix
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
When a \fIverb\fR that needs a playbook is not given one explicitly, Tangsible resolves one in order from:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
\fB$TANGSIBLE_PLAYBOOK\fR
.IP 2. 4
\fB.\&tangsible/config.\&toml\fR in the current directory
.IP 3. 4
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tangsible/config.\&toml\fR (default \fB~/.\&config/tangsible/config.\&toml\fR)
.IP 4. 4
\fB.\&/site.\&yml\fR, if present
.PD
.PP
Both config files share the same TOML shape:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[general]
default_playbook = "myplaybook\&.yml"
default_tree_state = "collapsed"   # "expanded" or "collapsed"
two_pane_layout = true             # default: true
color = true                       # default: true
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tangsible/config.\&toml\fR (default \fB~/.\&config/tangsible/config.\&toml\fR)
.RS 4
Global user settings.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB.\&tangsible/config.\&toml\fR
.RS 4
Project-local, user settings.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
The playbook completed successfully; completed with only unreachable hosts and no other failure; or the run was interrupted by the user (\fBq\fR or \fBCtrl-C\fR).\& None of these are treated as a Tangsible failure.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
The playbook genuinely failed (any exit code other than the two benign cases above), or the terminal UI itself errored.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage error: a required argument was missing, or no playbook could be resolved.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBstrategy: free\fR is not supported
.IP \(bu 4
Interactive playbook elements (e.\&g.\& a bare \fBpause\fR task or \fB--step\fR) are not supported
.IP \(bu 4
Execution environments are not supported
.IP \(bu 4
Tangsible is developed and tested against inventories on the order of ten hosts, not fleet scale.\&
.PD
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBansible-playbook\fR(1), \fBtangsible-run\fR(1), \fBtangsible-rerun\fR(1), \fBtangsible-role\fR(1), \fBtangsible-template\fR(1), \fBtangsible-host\fR(1), \fBtangsible-hosts\fR(1), \fBtangsible-revisit\fR(1), \fBtangsible-vault\fR(1)
